        acceptable; a broken tier 1 is not.

  controls:
    negcon_crispr_non_targeting: {jcp: JCP2022_800002, name: non-targeting, per_plate_wells: 10, verified: true}
    control_depth_warning: >-
      Only 10 non-targeting wells per CRISPR plate, versus 64-79 DMSO wells
      per TARGET2 plate. The knockout side is the noisier side. This is
      exactly why 7 replicate plates are mandatory and why gate_1 exists.
      Do not reduce the plate count to save download time.
    negcon_crispr_no_guide:      {jcp: JCP2022_800001, name: no-guide, verified: true}
    poscon_crispr:               {jcp: JCP2022_805264, name: PLK1, verified: true}
    rule: >-
      Normalize every knockout against the NON-TARGETING wells ON ITS OWN
      PLATE. Never against a pooled cross-plate control. Never against
      no-guide unless non-targeting is unavailable, and if you make that
      substitution you must record it in the FCO.

  orf_rescue_arm:
    status: TIER_3_OPTIONAL_AND_HAZARDOUS
    symbol: TAZ
    jcp: JCP2022_910418
    source: source_4
    batch: 2021_05_10_Batch3
    well: E16
    plates: [BR00123613, BR00123614, BR00123616, BR00123617, BR00123618]
    verified: true
    negcons: [JCP2022_915128 BFP, JCP2022_915129 HcRed, JCP2022_915130 LUCIFERASE, JCP2022_915131 LacZ]
